        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Swift is a cooperative of 11,000+ financial institutions with no on-chain governance; its blockchain experiments route through centrally controlled messaging infrastructure, meaning a single standards body controls adoption pace and access rules.",
          "source": "https://www.prosightfa.org/insights/what-is-swift-and-its-role-in-global-banking/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Swift operates under multi-jurisdictional oversight and has historically been weaponized for sanctions (Russia 2022); its digital asset pilots must navigate conflicting regulatory regimes across North America, Europe, and Asia simultaneously.",
          "source": "https://www.swift.com/news-events/news/swift-takes-bold-steps-unlock-benefits-digital-finance-global-scale"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Interoperability / Smart-contract",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Swift's blockchain layer relies on external oracle networks (primarily Chainlink) to bridge on-chain and off-chain state — any oracle failure, manipulation, or downtime introduces settlement risk that Swift's traditional SLA frameworks were not designed to handle.",
          "source": "https://chain.link/blog/the-swift-and-chainlink-partnership"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "Low",
          "note": "Swift moves an estimated $5 trillion daily across member banks; its tokenization pilots are additive rather than replacing existing liquidity pools, reducing transition-period liquidity fragmentation risk compared to greenfield DeFi protocols.",
